DEVIATION[dev-ftz-denormals]: subnormal (denormal) float32 *operands* are flushed to zero + subnormal (denormal) float32 *results* are flushed to (signed) zero
  scope: /: classes=['denormal_operand', 'denormal_result'] n=1456 max|d|=1.192e-07 max_ulp=872415232 beyond_tol=552; inv: classes=['denormal_result'] n=480 max|d|=2.939e-39 max_ulp=2097152 beyond_tol=0; loose_div: classes=['denormal_operand', 'denormal_result'] n=1200 max|d|=1.401e-36 max_ulp=65956648 beyond_tol=0; loose_inv: classes=['denormal_result'] n=480 max|d|=2.939e-39 max_ulp=2097152 beyond_tol=0; loose_pow: classes=['denormal_operand', 'denormal_result'] n=360 max|d|=2.670e+22 max_ulp=92274688 beyond_tol=128; loose_sqrt: classes=['denormal_operand'] n=880 max|d|=3.743e-23 max_ulp=439682291 beyond_tol=0; pow: classes=['denormal_operand', 'denormal_result'] n=296 max|d|=2.670e+22 max_ulp=92274688 beyond_tol=106; sin: classes=['denormal_operand'] n=880 max|d|=1.401e-45 max_ulp=1 beyond_tol=0; sinh: classes=['denormal_operand'] n=880 max|d|=1.401e-45 max_ulp=1 beyond_tol=0; sqrt: classes=['denormal_operand'] n=880 max|d|=3.743e-23 max_ulp=439682291 beyond_tol=440; tan: classes=['denormal_operand'] n=880 max|d|=1.401e-45 max_ulp=1 beyond_tol=0; tanh: classes=['denormal_operand'] n=880 max|d|=1.401e-45 max_ulp=1 beyond_tol=0
  root cause: the JIT-compiled kernel does not preserve subnormal operands (grid values and tree constants alike) -- they behave as 0.0 -- while reference_eval is correctly rounded and keeps them.  The deleted legacy CUDA engine was built with -use_fast_math (FTZ) too, so this is legacy-consistent but NOT oracle/ETL-consistent. results in the subnormal range (|r| < 1.1754944e-38) come out as 0.0 where the oracle returns the subnormal, e.g. inv(f32_max) = 2.9387359e-39 -> 0.0, pow(f32_max, -1) -> 0.0, 1.0/f32_max -> 0.0; same FTZ root cause as denormal operands.  Value-level impact is tiny (<= 1.2e-38, inside the documented atol) but it is visible in the payload bits and can flip a later op's class (e.g. through a comparison or a division).
  fixtures affected: False
  fixture-impact evidence: fixture gates green: True; special-value scan of both fixtures (fixture200.consts: n=828 zero=0 neg_zero=0 denormal=0 inf=0 nan=0; fixture200.labels: n=64 zero=0 neg_zero=0 denormal=0 inf=0 nan=0; fixture200.x: n=128 zero=0 neg_zero=0 denormal=0 inf=0 nan=0; fixture64.consts: n=160 zero=0 neg_zero=0 denormal=0 inf=0 nan=0; fixture64.labels: n=64 zero=0 neg_zero=0 denormal=0 inf=0 nan=0; fixture64.x: n=128 zero=0 neg_zero=0 denormal=0 inf=0 nan=0)
